[size=5]Description[/size]
Inventory space is a main limit in [i]Survival Log[/i], and a lot of playtime goes into fitting item shapes into the character bag and every storage. Compact Inventory removes the puzzle: every item takes one cell (1x1) in every bag grid. A large item such as Whole Lamb or Rack of Ribs takes the same one cell as a small item, so you manage inventory by item count and weight, not by shape.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Every bag is 1x1.[/b] The character bag, each storage, and every other panel that shows a bag grid.[/*]
[*][b]Existing saves included.[/b] Items already in a save become 1x1 the first time you load that save with the mod installed, at their saved position.[/*]
[*][b]Nothing else changes.[/b] Item weight, stack limits, bag sizes, trade value, and every other item stat or game rule stay the same. Only the grid size changes.[/*]
[*][b]No configuration.[/b] 1x1 is the only mode.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\CompactInventory.dll[/code]
[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]CompactInventory.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

Before you remove the mod, back up your save and give each large item its own free space in each bag, so items do not sit close together. Once the mod is gone, a full bag no longer has room for every item at its real size. In testing, the game's own load-repair moved what it could and dropped the rest on the ground next to the storage; no item was seen deleted, but the save was marked [font=Courier New]suspect[/font] in the game's own report. Making room before removal avoids this.

